# Generated artifacts that are compared byte-for-byte.
#
# `backend/openapi.json` is the committed frontend/backend contract. A test
# regenerates it and compares it to the committed copy, and a CI job will do
# the same, so a difference is supposed to mean "a backend route changed and
# the schema was not refreshed".
#
# With no attribute and `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on Windows — git
# checks that file out with CRLF while the export script writes LF. The
# comparison then fails on a fresh clone, on a machine where nothing is wrong,
# and reports it as contract drift. Measured: 2429 carriage returns introduced
# by a single checkout, and `test_committed_openapi_json_matches_a_fresh_export`
# red because of them.
#
# A gate that cries wolf on a clean checkout gets ignored, and this one is the
# only thing standing between a changed route and a silently broken TypeScript
# client.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `-text`: these stay diffable and reviewable, they are
# just never translated.
backend/openapi.json          text eol=lf
frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts  text eol=lf
